    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Lawrence Butler** (72.38) and **Bryce Harper** (71.31) headline our lineup as the most efficient plays. **Lawrence Butler** benefits from an aggressive matchup against Brady Singer, where a significant +13% dynamic platoon boost and a +3% park factor elevate him well above his base projection. Similarly, **Bryce Harper** anchors our heart of the order; despite a minor platoon disadvantage against Carson Palmquist, his elite 0.387 xwOBA and top-tier order placement make him a near-must-start. We are also capitalizing on the favorable park conditions and porous matchups for **Geraldo Perdomo** (69.91) and **Dylan Beavers** (69.52), both of whom are projected to thrive against Grayson Rodriguez, aided by a substantial +19% SP skill advantage.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was undoubtedly **Kyle Karros**. With a score of 61.33, he trailed the bottom of our active roster\u2014primarily **Gavin Sheets** and **Cal Raleigh**\u2014only by a thin margin. While **Kyle Karros** offers a solid park and order boost, the optimizer favored the higher volatility and specific defensive/platoon configurations of the active starters. Meanwhile, owners should remain cautious regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status for all players; specifically, **Jeremiah Jackson** and **Dylan Beavers** face the risk of a high-velocity threat in Grayson Rodriguez, and any shift in batting order could negatively impact their efficiency scores, particularly for those currently slotted lower in the lineup.\n\nFinally, while **Jung Hoo Lee** remains a name to watch due to his elite stolen base potential, his 46.99 score keeps him on the bench today against MacKenzie Gore. Even with a +2% boost for his speed against a slow-delivery pitcher, the combination of a tough opponent SP and a significant platoon disadvantage against the lefty keeps him outside the starting rotation. We are operating with a firm focus on efficiency metrics, banking on the high-upside matchups for **Jonathan Aranda** and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** to carry the offensive load while keeping our rostered depth ready to rotate as confirmed lineups crystallize.",
